                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">This course is organized into four modules based on the “normal-abnormal-mechanism-intervention-innovation” of the respiratory system:</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">1. Normal Structure and Function of the Respiratory System</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(1) Development and histology</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(2) Physiological Functions</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">2. Pathology and Pathogenesis of Respiratory Diseases</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(1) Infection and hypoxia</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(2) Obstructive and restrictive lung diseases</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(3) Tumors</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(4) Respiratory Failure</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">3. Intervention Strategies for Respiratory Diseases</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(1) Pharmacotherapy</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">(2) Non-pharmacological interventions:</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">4. Frontiers and cross-cutting areas</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Progress of research on the mechanisms of respiratory diseases and clinical diagnosis and treatment.</span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
